  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "One of the owners should reach out towards the developers to include this idea. With Meta’s new OS update (V68)basically killing performance on the Quest 2 (the most) and even the 3. This update uses way much more RAM and VRAM by a lot which can cause some VRChat worlds to load insufficiently and redirect players back to their home. With the new update, this has applied to a bunch of new worlds and causes for peformance to lack of variety with worlds that haven’t been updated. Even for worlds such as The Black Cat and Murder 4 causes lots of sudden battery drain and problems due to use of VRAM. And, with people bypassing making over 100MB+ avatars for quest (preferably X-rated avatars) its no surprise people wear them in public instances. That was already a problem. Now, it is just being caused by the loading of the worlds themselves and not user avatars (even ones below 90MB) and not avatars. Please add this as a Graphics Setting or Toggle for Android Users.",
